# The full gate, and the only one: lint, openapi + asyncapi lint, format check, the cross-repo
# contract check, build, Cypress e2e against the fixed mock dataset, and Cypress again against a
# freshly generated one.
#
# Around ten minutes, and that is accepted deliberately: the alternative is a lighter hook that
# lets a broken e2e run reach a push, and Cypress is the only layer here that exercises the app as
# a user meets it. Run it, or run `git commit --no-verify` knowingly — not by default.
#
# `check:spec-identity` SKIPS rather than fails when the paired backend is not on disk, so a
# half-cloned pair can still commit. It stays fatal under CI, where a missing sibling means the
# workflow is misconfigured rather than absent.
#
# Deliberately not here, and run by hand for the occasions that want them: `test:mutation`
# (re-executes the unit suite once per mutant — nightly in CI), and `complete:manual`, which is
# `test:e2e:visual` (pixel diffs that answer to the machine that took them) plus `test:e2e:live`
# (needs the paired backend up).
npm run complete
